.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=MarkFar
.Options CtrlStartPosChar=^<wrap>

@Contents
$ #MarkFar#
  Version @VERSION@

  MarkFar shows a Markdown file rendered: headings, emphasis, lists, quotes,
tables, links and code blocks with formatting and colour, wrapped to the
window width. Code blocks are coloured by the Colorer plugin.

  ~Opening the preview~@Open@
  ~Keys in the preview~@Preview@
  ~Settings~@Settings@
  ~Colorer and code blocks~@Colorer@

  MarkFar is free software under the BSD Zero Clause License, provided "as
is", without warranty of any kind.

@Open
$ #Opening the preview#
  #F11 → MarkFar# on a file in a panel opens its preview.

  #F11 → MarkFar# in the editor switches between the file and its preview.

  #markfar:<file># in the command line opens the preview of <file>.

  #F3# on a .md or .markdown file in a file panel opens the preview (setting
"F3 on a Markdown file..."). #Alt+F3# still opens Far's viewer.

  #markfar:<file># can also be used in a file association, for example for
other extensions: #F9 → Commands → File associations#, command for view (F3)
#markfar:!\!.!#.

  If the file is open in Far's editor, the preview shows the editor text,
including changes not saved yet.

@Preview
$ #Keys in the preview#
  The preview is Far's editor in locked mode: the usual keys for moving,
searching (#F7#) and copying work; the text cannot be changed.

  #F2#                   ^<wrap>Word wrap on or off.
  #F6#                   ^<wrap>Switch to the file in Far's editor, at the same place. #F6# in the editor of a Markdown file returns to the preview, showing the current text.
  #Ctrl+Down#            ^<wrap>Next heading.
  #Ctrl+Up#              ^<wrap>Previous heading.
  #Esc#, #F10#           ^<wrap>Close the preview. An open editor of the file stays open.
  #F1#                   ^<wrap>This help.

  When the window size changes, the preview is rendered again for the new
width.

@Settings
$ #Settings#
  #F9 → Options → Plugins configuration → MarkFar#

  #Word wrap in the preview#
  ^<wrap>Whether a new preview opens with word wrap. #F2# switches it in an open preview.

  #Show link URLs#
  ^<wrap>Shows the address after the text of each link.

  #F6 in a Markdown editor opens the preview#
  ^<wrap>When off, #F6# in the editor of a .md file opens Far's viewer, as usual.

  #F3 on a Markdown file in the panels opens the preview#
  ^<wrap>A macro that MarkFar adds when Far starts. When off, #F3# opens Far's viewer.

  #Colour code blocks with Colorer#
  ^<wrap>Registers #markfar.hrc# with Colorer, see ~Colorer and code blocks~@Colorer@.

@Colorer
$ #Colorer and code blocks#
  Code blocks with a language tag (#```sql#, #```csharp#, ...) are coloured
by the Colorer plugin through the scheme file #markfar.hrc#, which ships in
the #hrc# folder of the plugin. MarkFar registers it when Far starts (setting
"Colour code blocks with Colorer"):

  - ^<wrap>if Colorer's #Custom schemas folder (hrc)# is empty, MarkFar sets it to the plugin's #hrc# folder;
  - ^<wrap>if it already names another folder, MarkFar copies #markfar.hrc# into that folder.

  Switching the setting off undoes this. Colorer picks the change up after
reloading its schemes, at the latest after a restart of Far.

  Without Colorer, code blocks are shown in one colour.
